Anushri new code


Summary of New Panel Controls

Mode	Button / Combo	Action	LED Feedback
Playback / Idle	Hold + Synth	Load Sequence Memory 1 (EEPROM 0x0100)	Row 1 LED lights while Hold is held
Playback / Idle	Hold + Clk/Kbd	Load Sequence Memory 2 (EEPROM 0x01A1)	Row 2 LED lights while Hold is held
Playback / Idle	Hold + Drums	Load Sequence Memory 3 (EEPROM 0x0242)	Row 3 LED lights while Hold is held
Playback / Idle	Synth / Clk/Kbd	Switch Synth / Clk-Kbd knob pages as normal	Row 1 / Row 2 LEDs
Step Recording	Hold	Insert Tie (0xfe)	4-step bar LEDs advance
Step Recording	Drums	Toggle Slide Latch for the next note	Row 3 (Drums) LED lights while Slide is latched
Step Recording	Clk/Kbd	Insert Rest (0xff)	4-step bar LEDs advance
Step Recording	MIDI Key	Record note (applies & clears Slide Latch if armed)	4-step bar LEDs advance
(Note: Because Hold + Synth, Hold + Clk/Kbd, and Hold + Drums now select Memories 1–3, MIDI Channel Learn, MIDI Out Filter, and PPQN settings are untouched in system_settings or can be configured via SysEx—if you still want MIDI Learn, you can trigger it on power-up or remap it to Hold + Rec.)



File 1: anu/anu.cc (Complete Drop-In)
Removes drum_synth.Init(), drum_synth.Render(), and silences audio_out at 0 so the 39 kHz PWM carrier never bleeds into the analog audio path.

cpp
// Copyright 2012 Emilie Gillet.
